-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
System components (not bundled; invoked as separate programs)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Thimeo Stereo Tool (stereotool_cmd)
  Commercial, proprietary software by Thimeo Audio Technology.
  Not included, not redistributed. The station owner supplies the licensed
  binary, preset and license file (installed to /opt/stereotool and
  /etc/radio, mode 600). .gitignore blocks *.lic / *.sds / stereotool_cmd*.
  Use is subject to Thimeo's own license terms for the purchased edition.
  https://www.thimeo.com/stereo-tool/

FFmpeg (ffmpeg, ffprobe)
  LGPL-2.1-or-later; Debian's build is configured with GPL components, so the
  binary as installed is GPL-2.0-or-later. Used unmodified via the command
  line (decoding, encoding, loudness analysis); no FFmpeg code is linked into
  this project. Source: https://ffmpeg.org/ and the Debian source package.
  Note: MP3 (libmp3lame, LGPL-2.0) and AAC encoding are provided by the
  installed FFmpeg; MP3 patents have expired.

Icecast 2 (icecast2)
  GPL-2.0. Used unmodified as a separate streaming server; configuration is
  generated by `pnpm icecast:config`. Source: https://icecast.org/ and the
  Debian source package.

nginx — BSD-2-Clause. Certbot — Apache-2.0. SQLite (via better-sqlite3) —
public domain. Node.js — MIT (plus bundled third-party licenses).

Obligation review (M15.5): because FFmpeg and Icecast are only executed, not
linked or modified, and are obtained from Debian (which publishes the
corresponding source), distributing this repository creates no GPL/LGPL
source-offer obligation for those programs. Anyone who ships a pre-built image
or appliance that includes the FFmpeg/Icecast binaries must pass on their
license texts and a source offer (pointing at the Debian source packages is
sufficient). Thimeo Stereo Tool must never be included in such an image
without a redistribution agreement with Thimeo.

